  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Strengthened institutional capacity of employers&apos; organizations</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Nigerian Employers &#x2019;Consultative Association (NECA) is the voice of the business in Nigeria and as the world of work keeps evolving, so are the issues with private sector and business management and therefore, NECA is needed to provide tailor-made services to its members to enable them stay of top on the business environment including the workplace. Part of this is the environmental, social and governance (ESG) and in Nigeria reporting on ESG performance has become very important increasing pressure on companies to disclose this information. The ILO has developed a programme that is building the capacities of its social partners to function effectively. 

ILO strategy focuses on assisting NECA, to build its capacity so that it provides support to its member companies to implement and promote socially and environmentally good practices, operationalization of an e-learning training service and the delivery of information and sensitization on Violence and harassment</narrative>
  </description>
